<launch>
    <!-- The EKF: fuses the wheel odometry with the IMU's yaw rate (config/ekf.yaml), for the robot
         and the simulation alike. The EKF publishes its estimate on the topic
         /diffbot/odometry/filtered, and the transform odom → base_footprint on the topic /tf.
         Included, if ekf is true, by diffbot_base/launch/diffbot.launch on the robot and by
         diffbot_control.launch in the simulation. Both also turn off the drive controller's own
         transform odom → base_footprint, so that only one node publishes it.
         A figure of which launch file includes which:
         https://ros-mobile-robots.com/packages/imu/robot_localization/#which-launch-file-starts-what -->
    <group ns="diffbot">
        <!-- The IMU sample validator (scripts/imu_validator.py) forwards a sample from the topic
             imu/data_raw to the topic imu/data_validated, unchanged, only if the sample passes
             all five checks of the list below. The validator drops every other sample and
             counts the dropped samples on the topic /diagnostics. The script's docstring says
             more about each check.
             1. The sample's frame is frame_id, the IMU's frame in the URDF.
             2. Its angular velocity and its linear acceleration are finite numbers.
             3. The variances of its angular velocity are positive.
             4. Its stamp fits the ROS time, the validator's clock when the sample arrives:
                - The stamp is not more than max_age (0.1 s, five samples at the IMU's 50 Hz)
                  older than the ROS time. A sample takes time to travel from the Teensy
                  through rosserial, so its stamp is normally a little older. A sample that
                  waited long in a buffer is older than max_age.
                - The stamp is not more than max_future (0.02 s, one sample) ahead of the ROS
                  time. The Teensy stamps a sample with its own clock, which rosserial keeps
                  only roughly in step with the SBC's. The remaining offset between the two
                  clocks can put a stamp ahead.
             5. Its stamp is later than the stamp of the last sample that the validator
                forwarded -->
        <node name="imu_validator" pkg="diffbot_control" type="imu_validator.py" output="screen">
            <param name="frame_id" value="imu_link"/>
            <param name="max_age" value="0.1"/>
            <param name="max_future" value="0.02"/>
        </node>

        <node name="ekf_localization" pkg="robot_localization" type="ekf_localization_node" output="screen">
            <rosparam command="load" file="$(find diffbot_control)/config/ekf.yaml"/>
        </node>
    </group>
</launch>
